      "id": "CVE-2026-128117",
      "aliases": [
        "GHSA-mw6w-2fmv-pvw3"
      ],
      "title": "SvelteKit: Unhandled URIError when `reroute` rewrites a malformed pathname crashes adapter-node",
      "summary": "SvelteKit is a framework for rapidly developing robust, performant web applications using Svelte. Prior to versions 2.70.4 and 3.1.1, the reroute hook could rewrite an invalid percent-encoded pathname into a valid route and reach a comparison that decoded the original malformed pathname outside the guarded decoding operation. The resulting unhandled URIError could crash an adapter-node server and deny service to other requests. This issue is fixed in 2.70.4 and 3.1.1.",
      "published_at": "2026-11-13T19:29:04.744Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-11-13T21:22:10.163Z",
